---
import { Picture } from 'astro:assets';

import BrowserFrame from '../../components/BrowserFrame.astro';
import ArchitectureDiagram from '../../components/case-study/ArchitectureDiagram.astro';
import ScreenGallery from '../../components/case-study/ScreenGallery.astro';
import ExternalLink from '../../components/ExternalLink.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
import Tags from '../../components/Tags.astro';
import { FACETFLOW } from '../../data/projects';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const HERO_WIDTHS = [640, 960, 1280, 1800, 2400];
const HERO_SIZES = '(min-width: 72rem) 1120px, calc(100vw - 2rem)';
---

<BaseLayout title={`${FACETFLOW.name} case study · Abdullah Omar`} description={FACETFLOW.summary}>
  <article class="case-study">
    <header class="container case-study__header">
      <a class="case-study__back" href="/#work">
        <Icon name="arrow-left" size={14} /> All work
      </a>
      <p class="eyebrow">Case study · {FACETFLOW.years}</p>
      <h1 class="case-study__title">{FACETFLOW.name}</h1>
      <p class="case-study__lede">{FACETFLOW.summary}</p>

      <dl class="case-study__meta">
        <div>
          <dt class="eyebrow">Role</dt>
          <dd>{FACETFLOW.role}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="eyebrow">Stack</dt>
          <dd><Tags tags={FACETFLOW.tags} /></dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="eyebrow">Live</dt>
          <dd>
            <ExternalLink href={FACETFLOW.url} class="case-study__live">
              facetflow.io <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={14} />
            </ExternalLink>
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </header>

    <div class="container">
      <BrowserFrame>
        <Picture
          class="case-study__hero"
          src={FACETFLOW.hero.image}
          alt={FACETFLOW.hero.alt}
          formats={['avif', 'webp']}
          widths={HERO_WIDTHS}
          sizes={HERO_SIZES}
          loading="eager"
          fetchpriority="high"
          style="view-transition-name: shot-facetflow"
        />
      </BrowserFrame>
    </div>

    <div class="container case-study__body">
      <section aria-labelledby="problem">
        <h2 id="problem">The problem</h2>
        <p>
          Taking a piece of jewelry from a customer's idea to something priced and ready to manufacture means sketches,
          CAD, stone sourcing and spreadsheets, each in a different tool and often with a different person. Every
          revision goes round the same loop, and quoting a price can take days.
        </p>
        <p>
          FacetFlow puts that whole path in one place. A jeweler describes a design or uploads a sketch or photo, refines
          it in conversation, sees it worn, and gets a price for each quality tier, all without leaving the chat.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="role">
        <h2 id="role">What I built</h2>
        <p>
          I work directly with the founders as part of a small team, so I own features end to end, from the interface to
          the services and data behind it. Highlights:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>
            Design generation from prompts and reference images, with guided flows for refining a design version by
            version.
          </li>
          <li>Annotation, pricing and technical-drawing experiences that turn complex jewelry work into clear steps.</li>
          <li>Specialist agents and the tools they call, wired into one chat that plans every turn.</li>
          <li>The product details around them: usage-based billing, realtime progress, and reliable retries.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="architecture">
        <h2 id="architecture">How it works</h2>
        <p>
          Every request starts in one chat. A planner reads the turn and hands it to the specialist that fits, such as
          design or pricing. Each specialist runs its own loop of model calls and tools. All orchestration is built as
          LangGraph graphs, so a long run can pause for the user's approval and resume exactly where it stopped.
        </p>
        <ArchitectureDiagram />
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="trade-off">
        <h2 id="trade-off">One trade-off</h2>
        <p>
          AI calls are slow, billed, and sometimes fail halfway. The easy path is to retry them. We decided that every
          call to a paid or unpredictable provider goes through a single tool service that writes a durable receipt,
          keyed by a stable invocation key, before and after the call.
        </p>
        <p>
          The cost is more ceremony for each new tool. In return, a retry or a resumed run never charges a customer
          twice or generates the same render twice, and every step can be traced from the chat message down to the
          provider call.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="screens">
        <h2 id="screens">Screens</h2>
        <p>Select a screen to see it full size.</p>
        <ScreenGallery screens={FACETFLOW.screens} />
      </section>

      <footer class="case-study__footer">
        <a class="case-study__back" href="/#work">
          <Icon name="arrow-left" size={14} /> Back to all work
        </a>
        <ExternalLink href={FACETFLOW.url} class="case-study__live">
          Visit facetflow.io <Icon name="arrow-up-right" size={14} />
        </ExternalLink>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .case-study__header {
    padding-block: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem) 2.5rem;
  }

  .case-study__back {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.375rem;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .case-study__back:hover {
    color: var(--color-text);
  }

  .case-study__title {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-size: var(--text-display);
  }

  .case-study__lede {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: var(--text-lg);
  }

  .case-study__meta {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.25rem 3rem;
    margin-top: 2rem;
  }

  @media (width >= 48rem) {
    .case-study__meta {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.2fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr) auto;
    }
  }

  .case-study__meta dd {
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
  }

  .case-study__live {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .case-study__hero {
    width: 100%;
    aspect-ratio: 16 / 10;
    object-fit: cover;
    object-position: left top;
  }

  .case-study__body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 4rem;
    max-width: min(100% - 2 * var(--gutter), 55rem);
    padding-top: var(--space-section);
  }

  .case-study__body h2 {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    font-size: var(--text-h2);
  }

  .case-study__body section > p,
  .case-study__body section > ul {
    max-width: 44rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.25rem;
    color: var(--color-muted);
  }

  .case-study__body ul {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  .case-study__body li::marker {
    color: var(--color-accent);
  }

  .case-study__footer {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding-top: 2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }

  .case-study__footer .case-study__back {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
</style>
